{
  "version": 1,
  "_doc": "Style registry (loader: forms/kit.rs). kits.<id>.house = the home vocabulary of an architectural family: plans (weights of bar | ell | tee | court | cross | aitch), growth (0..1: how much room and wealth favour the larger plans), chances of the extras (outshot, porch, turret, bay, chimney, dormer), roofs (weights of the roof kinds of a home's bodies among gable | hip | halfhip | gablet | gambrel | mansard | saltbox; empty keeps the tradition's roof), overhang (eaves past the walls, m), stack (chimney material). A culture gets its kit from cultures.<culture id>.kit, else from the first derive rule its building traits match (roof kind, wall, cover, pitch range of its tradition), else from default. A new style needs no code: give it a kit here (or reuse one), its mass-role overrides in forms/roles_*.json, its monuments in services.json, and its tissue in catalogue.json. cultures.<culture id>.traits = the building traits the tissue does not carry (read by massing.rs, never by culture name; every field is optional and neutral when absent): tradition {roof: gable | hip | shed | pyramid | cone | tent | dome | barrel | flat, pitch (degrees), storeys [lo, hi], cover, wall, gableToStreet, form: yurt | tipi | stilt} = the roof tradition when the tissue declares no arch (absent: a plain tiled gable); mediterranean (low tiled roofs whatever the material, few small openings in masonry); flavor (roof-top detail family of flat roofs: maghreb | levant | persian | pueblo | meso; a flavored culture also has few small openings in masonry); bodyScale (inhabitants' size against a human; 0: human); metricScale (scale of the whole house; 0: 1); form (exterior form of homes: tree | mushroom | longhouse | yurt | battered | mage | stilt); formShare (share of the lots that take the form, the others keep the tradition; 0: all); massiveStorey (homes are one huge storey of massive stone under a flat roof); piles (homes stand on posts whatever their form); openness (facade openness 0..1 of every wall; 0: by climate and wall); lightWallOpenness (facade openness 0..1 of the non-masonry walls of a mediterranean or flavored culture; 0: fully open). A culture may have traits without a kit (its kit is then derived).",
  "_facets": "Reserved style facets, one entry per style id under `styles`, read by the stages as they migrate to this registry. Each facet names a source style or holds its own values, so a hybrid is a style whose facets come from different sources. houses: kit id (this file). monuments: services.json family and the role overrides of roles_*.json. rural: catalogue.json farmstead culture. siting: lot occupation (setback, side gap, courts, row | detached | perimeter | slab | tower-on-podium). plots: plot operator and dimensions (burgage | courtyard | compound | garden | whole block | superblock | cul-de-sac lots). streets: pattern (organic | grid | radial | superblock | curvilinear | cul-de-sac tree), hierarchy (widths by rank: arterial, collector, local, lane), block sizes. plan: nucleus, enclosure, zoning (centre, industry, housing, commerce, infrastructure corridors). regional: road classes between places (track | road | highway | motorway | rail) and their junctions. epochs: an ordered list of {style, share} for the growth phases of a place (an old core, a planned extension, an industrial belt, suburbs).",
